@startuml
!include ../themes/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' SPEC: _spec/_plans/android-p2p-wiring.puml
' purpose: Coach Android P2P — LanScreen consumes P2PClient; the Go server stays thin
' status: proposed 2026-09-17, not implemented; product = Coach Android
' covers: apps/ui/src/services/p2p.ts
'         apps/ui/src/screens/LanScreen.tsx
'         apps/android/app/src/main/java/ca/proveo/chess/android/MoveBridge.kt
'         apps/android/gomobile/thinserver/
' live spec: _spec/distribution.puml
'            _spec/apps/android/distribution.puml
'            _spec/apps/android/webrtc-p2p.puml
' ref: origin/feat-android (scaffold + remaining UI integration)
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── WHAT THE LINE ITEM SETTLES ─────────────────────────────────────────────
' Topology is already specified. The gap is WIRING: when
' ""isP2PAvailable()"", pair and relay through ""P2PClient"" /
' ""window.ChessNative"", and set ""capabilities().aiOpponent"" false
' so Maia does not answer a human peer.
'
' ── WHAT IT DOES NOT SETTLE ────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   WebRTC vs Tailscale (already in distribution.puml)
'   embedding Stockfish or WebLLM in the Go server
'   StarChess on Android
title PLANNED — LanScreen wires P2PClient;\nthe Go server stays a thin host

node "apps/android\nServerService · thinserver" as GO <<host>>
component "MoveBridge\nwindow.ChessNative" as BR <<host>>
component "apps/ui P2PClient\nservices/p2p.ts" as P2P <<app>>
component "LanScreen today\npeer.ts · signaling" as LAN <<app>>
component "capabilities\naiOpponent = false" as CAP <<app>>
component "**Go runs Stockfish**\nor a second pairing UI" as FORK <<error>>

GO ARROW_MAIN BR : loopback UI + tsnet
BR ARROW_MAIN P2P : injected bridge
LAN ARROW_OPTIONAL P2P : this plan when available
P2P ARROW_MAIN CAP : disable Maia reply
LAN ARROW_ERROR FORK : if it bypasses the bridge
GO ARROW_ERROR FORK : if the host becomes a coach

note bottom of LAN
  **""LanScreen"" today owns browser LAN
  (""HostHubTransport""), not Android.**
  ""P2PClient"" is store-agnostic and
  unused. feat-android names this gap.
end note

note bottom of GO
  **The embedded server is a thin host:
  static web-full, COOP/COEP, session,
  tailnet WSS.** It is not
  ""apps/server"" and not Maia.
end note

note right of FORK
  **A second pairing surface that still
  calls Maia teaches the wrong opponent.**
  One path: native bridge → game store
  ""addMoveSan"", AI reply off.
end note

legend bottom
  **The order to do it in**
  ==
  **1. Keep the live topology.** Read
  ""_spec/apps/android/distribution.puml""
  and ""webrtc-p2p.puml"". Do not redraw
  them in this file.
  --
  **2. Wire the existing screen.** When
  ""isP2PAvailable()"", ""LanScreen"" (or
  the LAN entry) uses ""P2PClient"":
  host/join, ""onPeerMove"" → ""addMoveSan"",
  ""aiOpponent === false"".
  ==
  **3. Validate on a device.** feat-android
  APK assemble is not runtime proof.
  WebGPU commentary stays optional.
  --
  **Left open**: Headscale vs auth keys;
  whether a dedicated Android pair screen
  replaces LAN chrome.
end legend
@enduml
